 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S444-021\", \"clauses\": {\"read\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"Read the fraction \\\\(\\\\frac{{{num}}}{{{den}}}\\\\). Which is the correct word name?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 asks the learner to read a fraction in notation as a word name. num comes from the one-member list [1] and den from the grade's denom_pool, so the read task is produced. Its options come from F14 and F19, which are failing families listed below; the read task itself is producible.\"}, \"write\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F11\", \"template\": \"Write {fraction_words} in fraction notation.\", \"reasoning\": \"F11 asks the learner to write a word name in fraction notation, so a write problem is produced. Its fraction_words come from nested family F14, which is a failing family listed below.\"}, \"unit_fractions\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F15\", \"template\": \"{num}/{den}\", \"reasoning\": \"F15 prints num from the one-member list [1] over den from denom_pool, so every F15 value is a unit fraction.\"}, \"fraction_notation\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"Which word name represents \\\\(\\\\frac{{{num}}}{{{den}}}\\\\)?\", \"reasoning\": \"F10 shows a unit fraction in fraction notation (num is the one-member list [1], den from denom_pool) as the item the learner names in words.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F11\", \"F12\", \"F13\", \"F14\", \"F17\", \"F19\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Write {fraction_words} in fraction notation.\", \"{den} {get}ths\", \"{den}/{num}\", \"{get} {ordinal}\", \"{v}/{den}\", \"{member}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F12 combines a denom_pool number with every member of _CARDINAL_WORDS plus the suffix ths. Several cardinals (one, two, three, five) are not stems that take that suffix, so the template can print non-words in options and distractors. F14 pairs any _CARDINAL_WORDS member with any member of _ORDINAL_WORDS (singular or with s). The domain has no agreement rule, so it can print plural-number phrases such as get member two with ordinal member halfs, or get member seven with ordinal member eighth. The list contains halfs, which is not a word. F11 nests F14, so its write prompt prints those phrases as well. F13 forms den over num with num fixed at 1, which yields whole-number fractions whose numerator exceeds the denominator. Improper fraction is listed in NOT_YET_KNOWN, so this is outside the lc's unit-fraction scope. F17 takes v from a range of 2 to 7 that is not tied to den, so with den 2 the domain allows v greater than den. Its basis says still below the denominator, but the declared bounds do not enforce that, and the output is fractions above one. F19 prints bank members that include invented word forms ending in oneths, improper values such as 7/6 and 9/8, and denominators 10, 12 and 16 outside denom_pool. F06, F10, F15 and F18 print only unit fractions or correct word names in their own templates and are not failing on their own text.\"}",
